<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.ralphnajm.AgentReview</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <name>Agent Review</name>
  <summary>Review the changes coding agents make</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Agent Review is where you review what your coding agent built. When it finishes, it asks you
      to review that version: you click through the running product, draw on screenshots of what
      needs changing, read the code changes, and hand the feedback back to the agent: post it for
      the agent to pull through MCP, or copy it to paste.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Switch between projects at any time</li>
      <li>Review the running product in an embedded browser, next to the code</li>
      <li>Draw on screenshots with a marker, arrows, boxes, sticky notes and text</li>
      <li>Read the code changes with syntax highlighting, and comment on lines and files</li>
      <li>Review a colleague's commit or pull request the same way, through your agent</li>
      <li>Post your review for your agent to pull, and see which comments it has resolved</li>
      <li>Or copy your feedback as Markdown, ready to paste into your agent</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.ralphnajm.AgentReview.desktop</launchable>
  <provides>
    <binary>agent-review</binary>
  </provides>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/ralphnajm/agent-review</url>
